# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone WAN / interface wan
#   zone LAN / interface lan
#   zone DMZ / interface opt1
#   zone GUEST / interface opt2
# Written inactive:
#   Servers fetch their updates: 'Updates' holds members only its platform knows
#   Mail out, not to the inside: not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'Web server HTTPS' (198.51.100.10, 192.168.20.10); not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'Application ports' (198.51.100.10, 192.16
#   Syslog to the collector: schedule 'OfficeHours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
#   Nothing from the list: references 'Blocklist': a URL table: its addresses are in a file on the firewall, not in the configuration
#   Phones of the guests: not converted: it matches a mark set by another rule (tagged) 'VOICE'
